# In-game help: item tooltips, and the JEI description pages.
tip.packagedautoterminals.terminal=This terminal lists the PackagedAuto machines of the ME network
tip.packagedautoterminals.terminal_use=Left click a group for a new recipe. Right click a recipe to edit it
tip.packagedautoterminals.wireless=This terminal does the same work, without a cable
tip.packagedautoterminals.wireless_link=Link it in an ME Security Terminal first
jei.packagedautoterminals.terminal.1=Place this part on a face of an ME cable. Then right click it. The terminal lists every Packager, every Unpackager and every Packaging Provider of the network. It joins the machines that work together into a group.
jei.packagedautoterminals.terminal.2=Left click a group row. The editor opens on a new recipe. Right click a recipe row to edit that recipe. The editor follows the layout of the Package Recipe Encoder. The ingredients sit on the left. The outputs sit on the right. Save writes the recipe into every machine of the group at the same time. The two sides stay equal.
jei.packagedautoterminals.terminal.3=The Machines tab reports every recipe that no crafter on the network runs. It lists the Package Crafters of the network below that report. A recipe holder carries twenty recipes at most, which is the limit of the Encoder itself.
jei.packagedautoterminals.wireless.1=The wireless terminal opens the same screen from anywhere in range. Link it in an ME Security Terminal first. Then right click with it, in either hand.
jei.packagedautoterminals.wireless.2=The wireless terminal draws power from its own buffer, like every other wireless terminal of AE2. Out of range or out of power, the screen closes. It does not show a network that it no longer reaches.
